<back><div type="verses">
<lg label="2."><l>“Preserve me, O God, for in Thee I confide”—</l><l>In God He took refuge whate’er did betide.</l><l>“O Thou art my Lord, I’ve no good beyond Thee”—</l><l>He spoke in Himself unto God constantly.</l></lg>
<lg label="3."><l>“As for all the saints who are dwelling on earth,”</l><l>To Him they’re the people of excellent worth.</l><l>Of them He has said He has all His delight—</l><l>In proving this all the four Gospels unite.</l></lg>
<lg label="4."><l>“The Lord is my portion, the Lord is my cup”—</l><l>For everything He to the Father looked up.</l><l>“The Lord I will bless who my counsel doth give”—</l><l>Himself He denied and by God’s word did live.</l></lg>
<lg label="5."><l>His heart thus was glad and His spirit rejoiced,</l><l>And e’en in His death praise to God could be voiced;</l><l>His soul God would never abandon to hell,</l><l>But in resurrection His body would dwell.</l></lg>
<lg label="6."><l>God raised Him, and He with God’s glory was crowned;</l><l>Then fulness of joy in God’s presence He found.</l><l>E’en now at the Father’s right hand is His seat,</l><l>Where flowing forever are pleasures complete.</l></lg>
</div>
</back>
</music></mei>
